{"questions":[{"question_id":"1lfyzljna","paperTitle":"IIT-JEE 2008 Paper 2 Offline","year":2008,"examDate":2008,"subject":"chemistry","chapter":"compounds-containing-nitrogen","chapterGroup":"organic-chemistry","topic":"diazonium-salts-and-other-nitrogen-containing-compounds","type":"mcq","marks":3,"negMarks":1,"permalink":"pstatement-1--aniline-on-reaction-with-nano2hcl-at-jee-advanced-chemistry-some-basic-concepts-of-chemistry-soqz1qyru3fvxcpc","content":"<p>Statement 1 : Aniline on reaction with NaNO<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.339ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"0.988ex\" height=\"1.065ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -320.9 436.6 470.9\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(33,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>/HCl at 0<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: 0;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"0.988ex\" height=\"1.532ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -677 436.6 677\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msup\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(33,363) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"2218\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2218\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>C followed by coupling with <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.439ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.296ex\" height=\"2.034ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -705 573 899\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D6FD\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D6FD\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>-naphthol gives a dark blue coloured precipitate.</p>\n<p>Statement 2 : The colour of the compound formed in the reaction of aniline with NaNO<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.339ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"0.988ex\" height=\"1.065ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -320.9 436.6 470.9\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(33,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>/HCl at 0<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: 0;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"0.988ex\" height=\"1.532ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -677 436.6 677\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msup\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(33,363) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"2218\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2218\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>C followed by coupling with <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.439ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.296ex\" height=\"2.034ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -705 573 899\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D6FD\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D6FD\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>-naphthol is due to the extended conjugation.</p>","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"Statement 1 is True, Statement 2 is True; Statement 2 is a CORRECT explanation for Statement 1."},{"identifier":"B","content":"Statement 1 is True, Statement 2 is True; Statement 2 is a NOT CORRECT explanation for Statement 1."},{"identifier":"C","content":"Statement 1 is True, Statement 2 is False."},{"identifier":"D","content":"Statement 1 is False, Statement 2 is True."}],"correct_options":["D"],"explanation":"<p>Let us discuss the given statements one by one.</p>\n<p>Statement 1 : Aniline reacts with NaNO<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.339ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"0.988ex\" height=\"1.065ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -320.9 436.6 470.9\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(33,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>/HCl at 273 K to form colourless diazonium salt.</p>\n<p><img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1lgewhtog/b8d3fc17-d073-430e-80b2-93b7fb860b1c/20ed4800-d9db-11ed-af1f-bf7b0ee7d77a/file-1lgewhtoh.png?format=png\" data-orsrc=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/1lgewhtog/b8d3fc17-d073-430e-80b2-93b7fb860b1c/20ed4800-d9db-11ed-af1f-bf7b0ee7d77a/file-1lgewhtoh.png\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;display:block;margin:0px auto;max-height:40vh\" alt=\"IIT-JEE 2008 Paper 2 Offline Chemistry - Compounds Containing Nitrogen Question 17 English Explanation 1\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/1lgewhtog/b8d3fc17-d073-430e-80b2-93b7fb860b1c/20ed4800-d9db-11ed-af1f-bf7b0ee7d77a/file-1lgewhtoh.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/1lgewhtog/b8d3fc17-d073-430e-80b2-93b7fb860b1c/20ed4800-d9db-11ed-af1f-bf7b0ee7d77a/file-1lgewhtoh.png?format=png 750w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1lgewhtog/b8d3fc17-d073-430e-80b2-93b7fb860b1c/20ed4800-d9db-11ed-af1f-bf7b0ee7d77a/file-1lgewhtoh.png?format=png 1000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1500/image/1lgewhtog/b8d3fc17-d073-430e-80b2-93b7fb860b1c/20ed4800-d9db-11ed-af1f-bf7b0ee7d77a/file-1lgewhtoh.png?format=png 1500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2000/image/1lgewhtog/b8d3fc17-d073-430e-80b2-93b7fb860b1c/20ed4800-d9db-11ed-af1f-bf7b0ee7d77a/file-1lgewhtoh.png?format=png 2000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2500/image/1lgewhtog/b8d3fc17-d073-430e-80b2-93b7fb860b1c/20ed4800-d9db-11ed-af1f-bf7b0ee7d77a/file-1lgewhtoh.png?format=png 2500w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) 100vw, 720px\" decoding=\"async\"></p>\n<p>Benzene diazonium chloride is then coupled with <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.439ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.296ex\" height=\"2.034ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -705 573 899\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D6FD\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D6FD\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>-naphthol to yield a dark red or orange coloured dye as shown in the reaction below:</p>\n<p><img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1lgewi7mn/557e6948-9f7d-4ca4-a5a9-483342c6c06a/2bb3eaf0-d9db-11ed-af1f-bf7b0ee7d77a/file-1lgewi7mo.png?format=png\" data-orsrc=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/1lgewi7mn/557e6948-9f7d-4ca4-a5a9-483342c6c06a/2bb3eaf0-d9db-11ed-af1f-bf7b0ee7d77a/file-1lgewi7mo.png\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;display:block;margin:0px auto;max-height:40vh\" alt=\"IIT-JEE 2008 Paper 2 Offline Chemistry - Compounds Containing Nitrogen Question 17 English Explanation 2\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/1lgewi7mn/557e6948-9f7d-4ca4-a5a9-483342c6c06a/2bb3eaf0-d9db-11ed-af1f-bf7b0ee7d77a/file-1lgewi7mo.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/1lgewi7mn/557e6948-9f7d-4ca4-a5a9-483342c6c06a/2bb3eaf0-d9db-11ed-af1f-bf7b0ee7d77a/file-1lgewi7mo.png?format=png 750w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1lgewi7mn/557e6948-9f7d-4ca4-a5a9-483342c6c06a/2bb3eaf0-d9db-11ed-af1f-bf7b0ee7d77a/file-1lgewi7mo.png?format=png 1000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1500/image/1lgewi7mn/557e6948-9f7d-4ca4-a5a9-483342c6c06a/2bb3eaf0-d9db-11ed-af1f-bf7b0ee7d77a/file-1lgewi7mo.png?format=png 1500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2000/image/1lgewi7mn/557e6948-9f7d-4ca4-a5a9-483342c6c06a/2bb3eaf0-d9db-11ed-af1f-bf7b0ee7d77a/file-1lgewi7mo.png?format=png 2000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2500/image/1lgewi7mn/557e6948-9f7d-4ca4-a5a9-483342c6c06a/2bb3eaf0-d9db-11ed-af1f-bf7b0ee7d77a/file-1lgewi7mo.png?format=png 2500w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) 100vw, 720px\" decoding=\"async\"></p>\n<p>Thus, the statement 1 is false as the colour of the precipitate formed is orange red not blue. As we have already seen in the above mentioned reactions that the colour compound (dye) formed in the reaction of aniline with NaNO<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.339ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"0.988ex\" height=\"1.065ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -320.9 436.6 470.9\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(33,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>/HCl at 0<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: 0;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"0.988ex\" height=\"1.532ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -677 436.6 677\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msup\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(33,363) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"2218\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2218\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>C was due to the successive coupling of diazonium salt with <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.439ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.296ex\" height=\"2.034ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -705 573 899\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D6FD\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D6FD\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>-naphthol. Hence, statement 2 is true.</p>\n<p>As a result, Statement 1 is False and Statement 2 is true.</p>"}]}